    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1013">

                <pb facs="0765" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13994.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-11T10:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 11, 1914, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The following is a textual translation of the telegraphic instruction sent to
                    Convention commander at Naco by General Gutiérrez in response to representations
                    of the Secretary of State in Department’s December 9, 1 p.m., to me.<anchor
                        n="84" xml:id="d1013-f1"/>
                </p>



                <xi:include href="d1013-a1.xml" xpointer="d1013-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1013-f1" n="84" xml:id="d1013-f1-content">
                <p>See last paragraph of Department’s telegram of that date to Mr. Canada.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
